## 2. FRED liquidity/breakeven batch — 7 net-new series
tools/quant/data/more_fred/ (keyed API via .env.local FRED_KEY; reused TDD'd fred_dl.py; 19 tests pass):
- WALCL (weekly, 2002+), RRPONTSYD (daily, 2015+ RRP-active era; pre-2015 sporadic = honest trim),
  SOFR (daily, 2018+), T10YIE + T5YIE (daily breakevens, 2003+),
  USEPUINDXD (daily policy uncertainty, 1985+, 15,220 obs), EMVOVERALLEMV (monthly EM vol, 1985+;
  mis-detected as daily at first — reclassified native monthly, zero gaps).
- UPGRADE documented: SP500/DJIA/DJCA via keyed API are STILL 10y-limited (FRED policy, not endpoint).
- Honest negatives: T5YIFP HTTP400 (discontinued upstream); MOVE already known-blocked.

## 3. ECB FX reference rates — 30 NEW series (keyless, full history)
tools/quant/data/ecb_fx/ (NEW dir; downloader ecb_fx_dl.py + 6 TDD tests, GREEN):
- 30 crosses vs EUR, daily, 1999-01-04 -> 2026-09-03 (~7,085 obs each):
  USD JPY GBP CHF AUD CAD NZD CNY HKD SGD KRW INR BRL MXN ZAR TRY SEK NOK DKK PLN CZK HUF RON BGN ISK IDR MYR PHP THB ILS
- ISK: ECB suspended 1999-2018 -> stored 2018+ era only (caveat in manifest).
- Value = units of CCY per 1 EUR (ECB 2:15pm CET reference). Existing fx/ block was only 8
  twelvedata pairs; this is the largest decorrelated expansion of the FX family available free.

